# Odysseus fork (odysseus-echo): key layout for the Echo Show 5 (2nd gen) privacy button.
#
# On LineageOS 18.1 (cronos) the microphone/camera privacy button is two input devices:
#   gpio-privacy-state   SW_MUTE_DEVICE  -> Android sets its microphone-mute flag (on this device
#                                           the microphone keeps working; the app ignores the flag
#                                           while the button is set to Record)
#   gpio-privacy-button  KEY_POWER (116) -> upstream: Android goes to sleep (not wanted)
# Here scancode 116 is MEDIA_RECORD instead of POWER, so the button never puts the device to sleep,
# and the app (MainActivity.dispatchKeyEvent -> odysseus/record/RecordButton.kt) turns its down and
# up into a press (record / stop) or a 1 s hold (voice note). Menu -> Odysseus -> Recording ->
# Privacy button: Mute makes the app swallow the key, so the button only mutes, as before.
#
# WAKE asks Android to wake the device on this key; Android 11 doesn't wake on media keys and
# doesn't pass any key to the app while the display is off. With the display off the app sees the
# press through the mute switch instead (no hold). See docs/odysseus/echo-show-5.md.
#
# Installed as /data/system/devices/keylayout/gpio-privacy-button.kl by setup_device.sh (not
# /system; InputReader checks /data/system/devices after /odm, /vendor and /system, which have no
# file for this device, before falling back to Generic.kl). Loaded at boot.
# Undo: delete the file, reboot (the button then puts the device to sleep again).

key 116   MEDIA_RECORD   WAKE
